ndamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Julia Letlow (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Julia Letlow's retirement to run for Senate leaves this heavily Republican northeast Louisiana seat open, but the district's R+17 partisan lean makes it a steep climb for any Democrat. State Representative Michael Echols leads the Republican field with nearly $3 million raised and over $1 million on hand, far outpacing rivals Misti Cordell and Gabe Firment. Democrat Dan McKay has raised only about $90,000 and reports negative cash on hand.\n\nPrediction markets give Republicans roughly a 94% chance of holding the seat, and no expert raters flag the race as competitive. Candidate forums in late September show active campaigning, but nothing suggests the partisan fundamentals are in doubt. The forecast expects a Republican hold by a wide margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -16.55}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0284, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0246, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0227, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0235, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.008, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.019, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0171, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0135, "margin": -17.0}]}